From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "NickLabs Orbis (port)" <orbis@nicklabs.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 12:57:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] PS4 HDMI audio: program the audio DTO in modeset; enable DIG1
 on ATI HDMI converters

Two community fixes for HDMI audio behind the PS4 DP->HDMI bridge, ported to 6.15.4:

- drm/amdgpu/dce8 (linux-psx 7.2-ps4 0175): the PS4 bridge path never runs
  afmt_setmode(), so DCCG_AUDIO_DTO0 stays at its reset value and all audio plays
  at ~0.615x speed (the "sample-rate defect"). Program DTO0 from the adjusted pixel
  clock in crtc_mode_set. linux-psx measured WALLCLK 14.778 -> 23.966 MHz and a 10 s
  48 kHz fixture 16.26 s -> 10.08 s (one boot on Baikal, acoustic check pending).
- ALSA hda/hdmi (linux-psx 0054, rmux): set AC_DIG1_ENABLE on the converters of codec
  0x1002aa01 at init; without it the bridge does not forward audio packets.
  In 6.15 the ATI HDMI code is sound/pci/hda/patch_hdmi.c (moved in 6.17).

Status: applies; not compiled or tested on a CUH-1215A by NickLabs Orbis.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 sound/pci/hda/patch_hdmi.c            | 15 +++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 31 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c
index 2973ca867..c0f979a50 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/dce_v8_0.c
@@ -2552,11 +2552,27 @@ static int dce_v8_0_crtc_mode_set(struct drm_crtc *crtc,
 				  int x, int y, struct drm_framebuffer *old_fb)
 {
 	struct amdgpu_crtc *amdgpu_crtc = to_amdgpu_crtc(crtc);
+	struct amdgpu_device *adev = drm_to_adev(crtc->dev);
 
 	if (!amdgpu_crtc->adjusted_clock)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	amdgpu_atombios_crtc_set_pll(crtc, adjusted_mode);
+
+	/* PS4: the DP->HDMI bridge path does not run afmt_setmode(), so the
+	 * audio DTO is never programmed.  The HDA controller uses DTO0 as its
+	 * 24 MHz reference; the reset value makes audio run at ~0.615x speed.
+	 * Program DTO0 from the active adjusted pixel clock here (same values
+	 * as dce_v8_0_audio_set_dto()).
+	 */
+	if (adev->asic_type == CHIP_LIVERPOOL || adev->asic_type == CHIP_GLADIUS) {
+		WREG32(mmDCCG_AUDIO_DTO_SOURCE,
+		       (amdgpu_crtc->crtc_id <<
+			DCCG_AUDIO_DTO_SOURCE__DCCG_AUDIO_DTO0_SOURCE_SEL__SHIFT));
+		WREG32(mmDCCG_AUDIO_DTO0_PHASE, 24 * 1000);
+		WREG32(mmDCCG_AUDIO_DTO0_MODULE, adjusted_mode->clock);
+	}
+
 	amdgpu_atombios_crtc_set_dtd_timing(crtc, adjusted_mode);
 	dce_v8_0_crtc_do_set_base(crtc, old_fb, x, y, 0);
 	amdgpu_atombios_crtc_overscan_setup(crtc, mode, adjusted_mode);
diff --git a/sound/pci/hda/patch_hdmi.c b/sound/pci/hda/patch_hdmi.c
index 7167989a8..f5777b834 100644
--- a/sound/pci/hda/patch_hdmi.c
+++ b/sound/pci/hda/patch_hdmi.c
@@ -4399,6 +4399,21 @@ static int atihdmi_init(struct hda_codec *codec)
 					    ATI_VERB_SET_MULTICHANNEL_MODE,
 					    ATI_MULTICHANNEL_MODE_SINGLE);
 	}
+
+	/* PS4 Liverpool (codec 0x1002aa01) behind the MN864729/MN86471A DP->HDMI
+	 * bridge: the bridge forwards audio only when AC_DIG1_ENABLE is set on the
+	 * converters (rmux, linux-psx 7.2-ps4 0054). */
+	if (codec->core.vendor_id == 0x1002aa01) {
+		int cvt_idx;
+
+		for (cvt_idx = 0; cvt_idx < spec->num_cvts; cvt_idx++) {
+			struct hdmi_spec_per_cvt *per_cvt = get_cvt(spec, cvt_idx);
+
+			snd_hda_codec_write(codec, per_cvt->cvt_nid, 0,
+					    AC_VERB_SET_DIGI_CONVERT_1,
+					    AC_DIG1_ENABLE);
+		}
+	}
 	codec->auto_runtime_pm = 1;
 
 	return 0;
